{"name":"Arrowhead","hex":"#514b40","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arrowhead","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The pointed part of an arrow (the weapon).","The pointed part of an arrow (the symbol)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrowhead"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arrowhead","blocks":[{"text":"An arrowhead or point is the usually sharpened and hardened tip of an arrow, which contributes a majority of the projectile mass and is responsible for impacting and penetrating a target, or sometimes for special purposes such as signaling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Fleche_Cartailhac_MHNT_PRE_2009.0.232.2_simple.jpg/330px-Fleche_Cartailhac_MHNT_PRE_2009.0.232.2_simple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrowhead"},{"title":"Arrowhead (Herman Melville House)","blocks":[{"text":"Arrowhead, also known as the Herman Melville House, is a historic house museum in Pittsfield, Massachusetts. It was the home of American author Herman Melville from 1850 to 1863. Melville wrote several of his major works at Arrowhead, including the novels Moby-Dick, Pierre, The Confidence-Man, and Israel Potter; The Piazza Tales ; and magazine stories such as \"I and My Chimney.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Arrowhead_%28Herman_Melville%29%2C_Pittsfield%2C_Massachusetts.JPG/330px-Arrowhead_%28Herman_Melville%29%2C_Pittsfield%2C_Massachusetts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrowhead_(Herman_Melville_House)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nydam_bone_arrowheads.jpg/500px-Nydam_bone_arrowheads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nydam_bone_arrowheads.jpg/1280px-Nydam_bone_a